    "details": "<p><strong>Hackathon to Solve India's Garbage Problem:</strong></p>\n<p>India generates over 150,000 tonnes of waste every day, and much of it ends up on streets, in drains, and in open dumps. It's a challenge that affects public health, quality of life, and the environment at a massive scale, and it needs bold, innovative solutions.</p>\n<p>That's where you come in. The <strong>AI First Product Builder Hackathon 2026</strong> is a free, nationwide, virtual hackathon where you use AI to build a cleaner Bharat: building AI-first software and hardware products that tackle India's garbage problem head-on.</p>\n<p><strong>Why Participate?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Work on a real-world problem that impacts millions.</li>\n<li>Build AI-powered solutions with genuine impact.</li>\n<li>Showcase your skills on a national platform.</li>\n<li>Win medals and certificates.</li>\n<li>Add a resume-worthy, impactful project to your portfolio.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What Can You Build?</strong></p>\n<p>Pick one of six tracks or combine them: civic education, street action, waste collection &amp; segregation, drain monitoring, recycling &amp; circular economy, or hardware &amp; IoT. Software, hardware, or both.</p>\n<p><strong>Who Can Join?</strong></p>\n<p>Everyone - you compete only within your division, judged fairly against peers: <strong>High School &middot; College &middot; Others</strong> (professionals &amp; graduates).</p>\n<p><strong>Key Details:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Registration opens:</strong> 20 July 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Submission deadline:</strong> 10 October 2026, 8:00 PM IST</li>\n<li><strong>Results:</strong> 17 October 2026</li>\n<li><strong>Free &middot; Virtual &middot; Solo or teams of up to 2</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Build something India actually needs.</p>",
